LQS = [
    (_q('Define demography?', 'ڈیموگرافی کی تعریف کریں۔', 'ډیموګرافي تعریف کړئ.'), 'Demography (Greek, "description of people") is the study of human populations: their size and composition and the movement of people from one region to another, together with the effects of population growth and its control; its key variables are fertility, mortality and life expectancy, migration, urbanization and carrying capacity.'),
    (_q('Differentiate between birth rate and death rate.', 'شرحِ پیدائش اور شرحِ اموات میں فرق کریں۔', 'د زېږون او مړینې کچې ترمنځ توپیر وکړئ.'), 'Crude birth rate = live births in a year / total population x 1,000 (births per thousand people). Crude death rate = deaths in a year / total population x 1,000 (deaths per thousand people). Birth rate adds to and death rate subtracts from a population; their difference is the natural growth rate.'),
    (_q('What do you mean by infant mortality rate?', 'شیرخوار بچوں کی شرحِ اموات سے کیا مراد ہے؟', 'د شیدې خوړونکو ماشومانو د مړینې کچه څه ده؟'), 'The number of deaths among infants under age one for each 1,000 live births in a year. A low infant mortality rate correlates with a higher life expectancy (the average lifespan of the population).'),
    (_q('Define the term migration. Differentiate between immigration and emigration.', 'نقل مکانی کی تعریف کریں اور امیگریشن اور ایمیگریشن میں فرق کریں۔', 'کډوالي تعریف کړئ او د امیګرېشن او ایمیګرېشن توپیر وکړئ.'), 'Migration is the movement of people from one place to another (voluntary or involuntary). Immigration is migration into an area, measured as people entering per 1,000 population; emigration is migration out of an area, measured as people leaving per 1,000 population. Internal migration takes place within a country\'s borders.'),
    (_q('What is the significance of carrying capacity of an area?', 'کسی علاقے کی گنجائش کی کیا اہمیت ہے؟', 'د یوې سیمې د ظرفیت اهمیت څه دی؟'), 'Carrying capacity is the maximum number of people (or animals) an area can support with its resources; e.g. a goat needing 50 sq yards of grass means 200 sq yards supports 4 goats. For humans it is more complex because technology, imported resources and infrastructure can raise it. When it is exceeded people leave, health and reproduction decline, pressure can lead to war, and unsanitary crowding causes disease outbreaks and environmental degradation; overgrazing beyond a grassland\'s capacity causes desertification.'),
    (_q('What do you mean by population growth? Give a comparative account of population growth of Pakistan and its neighbors.', 'آبادی میں اضافے سے کیا مراد ہے؟ پاکستان اور ہمسایوں کی آبادی میں اضافے کا موازنہ کریں۔', 'د نفوس وده څه ده؟ د پاکستان او ګاونډیو د نفوس ودې پرتله ولیکئ.'), 'Population growth is the change in size due to fertility, mortality and migration; natural growth rate = crude birth rate - crude death rate. Table 4.3: China births 12.2, deaths 6.9, 1,300 million, growth 0.49%; Pakistan 25.1, 7.1, 177.2 million, 1.51%; Bangladesh 23.8, 9.1, 158.1 million, 1.27%; India 21.3, 7.5, 1,100 million, 1.38%; Afghanistan 40, 15, 29.121 million, 2.21%. So Afghanistan grows fastest and China slowest, and Pakistan grows faster than India, Bangladesh and China.'),
    (_q('How does overpopulation have its impact on agriculture and forests?', 'زیادہ آبادی زراعت اور جنگلات پر کیسے اثر ڈالتی ہے؟', 'ډېر نفوس پر کرنه او ځنګلونو څه اغېز لري؟'), 'Agriculture: the need for more food leads to extensive cultivation that destroys habitats; canals cause waterlogging and salinity; overuse of fertilizers pollutes soil and water and pesticides make water toxic; genetically altered crops deplete soil; clearing land and excess irrigation cause erosion and silting that shortens dam life (Tarbela now has two-thirds capacity). Forests: they are cut for roads and houses, cultivation, pastures, timber and fuel wood, causing soil erosion, habitat loss, extinction, floods, climate change and desertification.'),
    (_q('Sustainable development is key to survival in this modern day world. Evaluate the statement critically.', 'پائیدار ترقی جدید دنیا میں بقا کی کلید ہے۔ تنقیدی جائزہ لیں۔', 'دوامداره پرمختګ په نننۍ نړۍ کې د بقا کیلي ده. په انتقادي ډول یې وارزوئ.'), 'Resources (fossil fuels, water, forests, food) are limited and being depleted, so they must be used to meet present needs without compromising future generations (WCED definition; Rio Earth Summit 1992). Rapid population growth in poor countries makes this hard: it blocks poverty reduction, causes unmanaged exploitation and environmental degradation, strains health and nutrition, and raises unemployment, inflation and political instability. Therefore sustainable development, together with population control, is essential; without controlling population, prosperity remains a dream.'),
]
